[{"id":"loop-predict-first","itemId":"loop-counter","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"Lesson 12.3's <code class=\"nobreak\">nest_count</code> with NOG = 3 output groups, T = 2 taps and NIG = 2 input groups; <code class=\"nobreak\">og</code>, <code class=\"nobreak\">tap</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">ig</code> are drawn. <code class=\"nobreak\">first</code> is 1 in each cycle that starts a new sum, from the bias. Cycles 0 and 1 are drawn for you. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">first</code> for the rest.","explanationHtml":"<p>A sum belongs to one output group and gathers every tap and input group of it, so it starts where <code class=\"nobreak\">tap</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">ig</code> are both 0: in cycles 0, 4 and 8, as <code class=\"nobreak\">og</code> becomes 0, 1 and 2. In between, <code class=\"nobreak\">ig</code> and then <code class=\"nobreak\">tap</code> count on within the same group. In cycle 12 <code class=\"nobreak\">busy</code> is 0, and so is <code class=\"nobreak\">first</code>.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"loop-first","source":"hdl/level-12/nest_count/nest_count_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":13,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"nest_count_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"],[8,"1"],[8.5,"0"],[9,"1"],[9.5,"0"],[10,"1"],[10.5,"0"],[11,"1"],[11.5,"0"],[12,"1"],[12.5,"0"]]},{"label":"busy","path":"nest_count_tb.busy2","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[12,"0"]]},{"label":"og[1:0]","path":"nest_count_tb.og2","width":2,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"00"],[4,"01"],[8,"10"]]},{"label":"tap[1:0]","path":"nest_count_tb.tap2","width":2,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"00"],[2,"01"],[4,"00"],[6,"01"],[8,"00"],[10,"01"],[12,"00"]]},{"label":"ig[1:0]","path":"nest_count_tb.ig2","width":2,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"00"],[1,"01"],[2,"00"